    "Orchestrate the full representation-aware constructive programme for four-dimensional Yang--Mills existence and the mass gap, from target freezing through RG, continuum limits, OS reconstruction, calibration, mechanization, and frontier audit. Use for end-to-end research planning or execution where every phase must have explicit gates and epistemic status.",
    "---\nname: ym-run-clay-program\ndescription: Orchestrate the full representation-aware constructive programme for four-dimensional Yang--Mills existence and the mass gap, from target freezing through RG, continuum limits, OS reconstruction, calibration, mechanization, and frontier audit. Use for end-to-end research planning or execution where every phase must have explicit gates and epistemic status.\n---\n\n## Abducer Integration Guards\n\n- Activate this skill only for `yang-mills-existence-and-mass-gap-target` or an explicitly marked Yang-Mills calibration task.\n- Treat imported representational-dynamics artifacts as restricted, finite, conditional, or support evidence unless a later proof discharges their frontier hypotheses.\n- Emit claim level, non-claims, hard gate, hypotheses, falsifier, and demotion trigger before any promotion.\n- Compose with the target-neutral proof-depth skills: pressure formalization, hard-gate selection, nontriviality audit, anti-definitionality audit, same-domain transfer certification, and declarative learning extraction.\n- State efficient representation requirements: preserved observables, morphisms or recovery maps, invariants, error budgets, equivalence policy, locality or cutoff budget, transfer interface, and falsifiers.\n- Do not let a transfer theorem pass if the target property is built into the bridge definition; require independently stated source and target objects plus a consequence delta.\n- Preserve the four-cycle, recursion-depth-one publication-consolidation limit for local subgoals.\n- Source provenance: `agentic/external/yang_mills_representational_dynamics/2026-07-20/skill_bundle/11_vscode_codex_skill_bundle/.agents/skills/ym-run-clay-program/SKILL.md`.\n- Apply the 2026-07-21 target overlay only after the current-literature rebase hook passes. Treat its ten hypothesis streams as incumbent-program evidence under the reflective conceptual parent, not as proof of conceptual plurality.\n- Reuse the existing guarded programme and add only `ym-prove-adaptive-block-domination`, `ym-prove-state-weighted-defect-transfer`, and `ym-prove-conditional-partition-ratio` from `agentic/external/yang_mills_representational_dynamics/2026-07-21/active_snapshot/`; keep its publication skills external-only.\n\n## Mathematical Invariants\n\nPreserve the Yang--Mills mathematical object: compact simple gauge group, pure gauge content, gauge-invariant observable algebra, regulator/cutoff/volume/coupling regime, reflection positivity, locality, OS reconstruction route, continuum limit order, and Hamiltonian spectral target. Any representation, morphism, RG step, or restricted model must state which invariants are preserved, which error budgets are allowed, and which edge case or counterexample would break transfer.\n\n## Epistemic Discipline\n\nEvery output must state epistemic status, claim level, evidence citation, source artifacts, explicit unknowns, and validation handoff. Treat physical relevance, literature-gap warrant, and frontier comparison as hard gates; unsupported implications stay conditional, blocked, or `requires_prior_art`.\n\n## Failure/Demotion\n\nDemote or quarantine if the skill assumes a mass gap, clustering, confinement, continuum existence, regulator independence, positivity, locality, observable density, or theory identity instead of proving it. Disconfirming evidence, prior-art collision, target-equivalent bridge definitions, or missing counterexample tests block promotion to a major YM publication pathway.\n\n# Run Yang--Mills Clay Programme\n\n## Mission\n\nCoordinate the complete theorem chain without letting conceptual reformulation substitute for the missing analytic estimates. Default to a regulator-agnostic atlas; prior Wilson-action work is optional and used only for a necessary comparison or calibration.\n\n## Phase Order\n\n1. Use `ym-freeze-clay-target` to state the exact existence-and-gap target and claim hierarchy.\n2. Use `ym-build-observable-core` to freeze the physical observable algebra and density obligations.\n3. Use `ym-build-representation-calculus` to type representations, morphisms, certificates, and error budgets.\n4. Use `ym-design-regulator-atlas` to select or compare regulator families.\n5. Use `ym-define-relational-rigidity` and falsify it on the counterexample bank.\n6. Use `ym-prove-rigidity-transfer` to prove the conditional spectral bridge.\n7. Use `ym-build-gauge-covariant-rg` and `ym-control-large-fields-and-topology` to construct the multiscale engine.\n8. Use `ym-design-infrared-basin` and `ym-prove-rg-to-rigidity` to isolate a noncircular sufficient mechanism.\n9. Use `ym-prove-adaptive-block-domination`, `ym-prove-state-weighted-defect-transfer`, and `ym-prove-conditional-partition-ratio` as alternative conditional one-scale routes. Preserve conflicts; none may certify the others by shared vocabulary.\n10. Use `ym-prove-basin-entry` to attack the central four-dimensional frontier theorem.\n11. Use `ym-prove-continuum-coherence` and `ym-reconstruct-os-gap` to construct and interpret the continuum theory.\n12. Use `ym-calibrate-restricted-models` and `ym-mechanize-proof-core` throughout as secondary support, not only at the end.\n13. Use `ym-audit-frontier` before raising any claim level.\n\n## Persistent Ledgers\n\nMaintain a theorem dependency graph, parameter registry, limit-order ledger, representation certificate table, observable-completeness ledger, counterexample bank, evidence ledger, and claim-status table. Each claim is `proved`, `imported`, `conditional`, `failed`, or `open`.\n\n## Phase Gates\n\nDo not advance a claim past a failed gate. Positivity, physical-unit uniformity, full-measure control, observable density, theory identity, continuum convergence, or regulator independence cannot be repaired by rhetoric downstream. Continue by proving a restricted theorem or identifying the first missing inequality.\n\n## Output Contract\n\nProduce a self-contained paper or dossier with definitions, proved and conditional theorems, counterexamples, executable artifacts, primary-source comparisons, and an explicit frontier statement. Claim `C6` only when every link of the Clay target is closed for every compact simple gauge group; otherwise state the strongest lower level precisely.\n\n## Packaged PRISM Output Contract\n\nReturn exactly the generated `ContinuumBoundaryAuditInput` JSON object. Do not paraphrase closed variant values.\n\n- Follow the exact generated JSON schema without extra fields.\n",
